# Jira Test issues and CI output

## Creating Test issues in Jira

Edit the table for your instance.

| What | Value |
|------|--------|
| **Project key** | `EPMRPP` |
| **Issue type** | `Test` |
| **Priority** | `Major` |
| **Label** (mark AI-generated Tests) | `ai-generated` |
| **Test Steps** field (preconditions + steps) | `customfield_19206` |
| **Expected result** field | `customfield_19207` |
| **Test Library** (TM / library scope; UI may show as library) | `customfield_24000` |
| **Folder** (path under library; UI may show as “Folder”) | `customfield_24001` |

Field ids for **`customfield_19206`**, **`customfield_19207`**, **`customfield_24000`**, **`customfield_24001`** were confirmed via **`jira_get_issue`** on sample Test [EPMRPP-114175](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114175) (`fields=*all`). On that issue, **`customfield_24000`** = `Test Library` and **`customfield_24001`** = `EPMRPP` (project-root folder only). **Do not** use that sample as the folder **target**—see **Test Folder (required)** below.

### Test Folder (required)

- **Do not** leave AI-generated Tests at the **EPMRPP project root** folder only. **`customfield_24001`** must reflect the team layout **`EPMRPP` → `AI Generated` → `<STORY_KEY>`** (not bare `EPMRPP` when the standard is the nested path).
- **`<STORY_KEY>`** is the same canonical story key as elsewhere in this rule (parent when dispatch was a Sub-task).
- Keep **`customfield_24000`** consistent with project practice (e.g. `Test Library` on [EPMRPP-114175](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114175)) unless your instance requires a different library value.
- If the folder **`AI Generated` / `<STORY_KEY>`** does not exist yet, create it under **`AI Generated`** in Jira Test Management (UI or whatever API your org supports) before or when filing Tests.

### MCP create / update (custom fields)

On **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`** (mcp-atlassian) or equivalent, pass **`customfield_19206`** (Test Steps), **`customfield_19207`** (Expected result), **`customfield_24000`** (Test Library), and **`customfield_24001`** (Folder) using the **same value types** Jira returns for a reference Test already filed in the **target** folder (**preferred**). If needed, use **`jira_get_field_options`** for **`customfield_24001`** with **`project_key=EPMRPP`** and **`issue_type=Test`** to obtain valid option ids or path strings. Exact format for the nested path (slash-separated string vs id) is instance-specific—**verify** with **`jira_get_issue`** on any Test already under **`EPMRPP / AI Generated / <some story key>`**.

Use these in **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`** (mcp-atlassian) or equivalent (**`jira_createIssue`** / **`jira_updateIssue`**). **Every** new Test must include the **`ai-generated`** label and **`priority: Major`** when your Jira setup allows it.

**Create and link** Test issues **only via Jira MCP**. No REST publish path in this pipeline.

### Linking Tests to the Story (required)

After creating or updating each Test issue, perform **both** of the following:

1. **Issue link — relation `is tested by` (Story → Test):** The link must read as **Jira Story (`STORY_KEY`) → `is tested by` → Test ticket** (the Test issue is what tests the story; on the Story issue, the link section shows **is tested by** pointing to each Test). Call **`jira_create_issue_link`** (or equivalent) with link type **`is tested by`** so **`STORY_KEY`** is the **source** side of that relationship and the **Test** issue key is the **target**—match your Jira instance’s inward/outward issue parameters for that link type (verify with **`jira_get_issue`** on a manually linked example if the API shape is unclear).
2. **Requirement field:** Set the Jira **Requirement** field on the Test to **`STORY_KEY`** (the story issue key). The field id may vary by instance—verify with **`jira_get_issue`** on a reference Test that already has a Requirement set (`fields=*all`); look for a field whose value is an issue-picker object pointing to a story. Pass the same value shape when calling **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`**.

Both steps apply to **newly created** and **updated** (existing) Test issues alike. If the MCP tool does not support one of these operations, try alternatives your MCP exposes; continue best-effort. **Do not** describe linking/Requirement/MCP limitations in the **completion comment** on **`STORY_KEY`** after tests are synced (**Story comment after successful test generation**).

### Sync with existing Jira Tests (no duplicates)

Whenever test generation runs against a story that may already have **Test** issues.

1. **After** the **Pre-generation MCP gate** passes, **before** bulk **`jira_create_issue`**, discover Tests already **linked** to **`STORY_KEY`**: e.g. **`jira_get_issue(STORY_KEY)`** with **`issuelinks`** (links where the story is **is tested by** the Test, or equivalent names per instance: **Tests** / **is tested by** / **tested by** / **tests**), and/or **`jira_search`** / JQL your MCP supports to list **Test** issues tied to that story.
2. **Do not** create a second Test for the same logical case. Match existing issues to planned **`tests[]`** rows by **Jira Test Summary** ↔ **`tests[].summary`** (normalize for comparison: trim, case-insensitive). When a match exists, use **`jira_update_issue`** to refresh **summary**, **`customfield_19206`**, **`customfield_19207`**, **`customfield_24000`**, **`customfield_24001`**, **`labels`**, and any other fields you maintain—**do not** **`jira_create_issue`** again for that row.
3. Use **`jira_create_issue`** **only** for planned tests that have **no** matching linked Test; after creation apply both linking steps from **Linking Tests to the Story** (relation type `is tested by` + Requirement field).
4. Do **not** assume an empty Jira side when re-running the pipeline; always **read linked Tests first**, then **update or add**.

## Cursor Agent CLI (headless)

- Run **`cursor-agent` / `agent`** **only** in **GitHub Actions** for this repo’s generate workflow (**`--trust`**, **`--approve-mcps`**, **`--force`**). **Do not** add scripts/docs that run the headless agent locally. **No** blocking questions. **Style:** **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`**; **shape:** **`.cursor/skills/jira-story-test-cases-md/SKILL.md`**. MCP setup: **`docs/GITHUB_SECRETS.md`**, **`docs/JIRA_MCP_OPTIONS.md`**, **`npm run render-mcp`**.

## Always use **STORY_KEY** — verify first

- **CI:** **`ISSUE_KEY`** = dispatch target; **`STORY_KEY`** = workflow-resolved story (parent when target is Sub-task). If they **differ**, **`ISSUE_KEY`** is **trigger only**. Scope: **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** only — description, summary (title context), AC/DoD fields. **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`** and Test **links** use **`STORY_KEY`**; **`tests[].summary`** (test case **names**) must **not** contain **`STORY_KEY`** or the Sub-task **`ISSUE_KEY`** when they differ (**`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`**).
- **IDE:** User may paste a Sub-task. **`jira_getIssue`** → if Sub-task, **`STORY_KEY = parent.key`**, then fetch the story. Never use Sub-task **description**/**summary** for scenarios when the story is the parent.

## Pre-generation MCP gate (before any tests)

**Before** authoring tests or writing **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/tests.json`**, use **Jira MCP** to call **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** (or equivalent) and load at least Jira **`summary`**, **`description`**, **`issuetype`**, **`parent`**, and AC/DoD-style fields if available.

- **Gate passes** when: the MCP call **succeeds**; the Jira issue **`summary`** (the **issue title** in Jira—**not** the **`tests[].summary`** field you write in **`tests.json`**) is a **non-empty** string; **`description`** is **present** in the response (value may be null, empty, or empty ADF).
- **Only after the gate passes:** derive tests, write **`tests.json`**, sync Jira Tests (see **Sync with existing Jira Tests**), or apply **Empty story** (below) if description + AC are genuinely empty.

**Failed gate (MCP error, missing tool, auth/network failure, missing/empty Jira `summary`):** **CI must fail.** **Do not** write **`tests.json`** or **`meta.json`**. **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** exits non-zero when **`tests.json`** is missing under **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`**, so GitHub Actions shows the job **failed** (red). **Never** use **`tests: []`** + empty **`meta.json`** to simulate success.

## Story-linked Confluence and Figma (MCP reads)

**After** the **Pre-generation MCP gate** passes and you have **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** (or equivalent), **before** you finalize test coverage, check whether the story references **Confluence** or **Figma** by URL.

**Where to look:** Jira **`description`** (plain text or extract link targets from ADF if your tools support it), AC/DoD-style custom fields, and—if you fetch them via Jira MCP—**comments** on **`STORY_KEY`**.

### When Confluence links appear

- Typical signals: hostnames or paths for your Confluence instance (e.g. **`/wiki/`**, **`confluence.`**, org knowledge-base hosts), page links embedded in the description or AC.
- Use **Confluence** read/search tools from the **Atlassian MCP** server (**`atlassian`** in **`.cursor/mcp.json`**). Exact tool names depend on the server build—use whatever Confluence tools the session exposes (get page, search, etc.).
- **Read-only:** use MCP to pull content needed to understand acceptance criteria, flows, or copy **referenced by the link**. **Do not** invent details that exist only on the linked page without fetching it when the link is present and MCP is available.

### When Figma links appear

- Typical signals: **`figma.com`** URLs (e.g. **`/file/`**, **`/design/`**) including file key and, when present, node/frame identifiers.
- Use tools from the **Figma MCP** server (**`acuvity-mcp-server-figma`** in **`.cursor/mcp.json`**). Use whatever read tools the session exposes so UI-oriented tests align with design intent (layout, labels, states) when the story points to a file or frame.

### If there are no such links

- **Do not** call Confluence or Figma MCP for exploration unrelated to URLs found on the story.

### If links exist but MCP read fails

- Optional context only: **do not** fail the whole run or treat this as a failed **Pre-generation MCP gate**. Complete tests from Jira text. **Do not** mention Confluence/Figma read failures in the **completion comment** on **`STORY_KEY`** after tests are generated (**Story comment after successful test generation**). **Never** put tokens or secrets in **`generated/`** or repo files.

## Jira fetch required (not the same as empty story)

This section aligns with the **Pre-generation MCP gate** above.

- **Empty story** (below) applies **only** after **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** **succeeds** (gate passed) and you have **actually read** the story’s **description** and AC/DoD-style fields from the response.
- If **Jira MCP is unavailable**, **`jira_getIssue`** **fails**, or the **gate** does not pass: **do not** treat that as an empty story. **Do not** write **`tests: []`** + **`meta.json`**. **Do not** produce a result that looks like a successful empty-story outcome.
- **CI:** Use **Generate Test Cases** on GitHub Actions (rendered **`.cursor/mcp.json`** + secrets) or **Cursor IDE** with working Jira MCP. If you cannot pass the gate, **omit** **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/tests.json`** so **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** fails; **never** substitute guesses or Sub-task text for the story body.

## Empty story — **do not** create tests

**No testable content** when **description** is empty (incl. empty ADF) **and** AC/DoD-style fields you fetched are empty—**after** the **Pre-generation MCP gate** passed (successful **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`**). **Jira `summary` alone** is not enough to invent scenarios when description + AC are empty.

Then: **`tests: []`**, **`meta.json`** with **`"jiraPublish": "mcp"`**, **`"mcpCreatedKeys": []`**. No **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_createIssue`**. No Sub-task backfill.

## Output directory

**Only** **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`**. **`STORY_KEY`** = story used for requirements (in CI: parent when input was Sub-task).

## `tests.json`

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "tests": [
    {
      "summary": "string (required)",
      "testSteps": "string (Preconditions + Steps as plain text for Jira Test Steps field)",
      "expectedResult": "string (maps to Expected result custom field)",
      "description": "optional Markdown"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **`summary`:** Plain EPMRPP title only—**do not** put **`STORY_KEY`** or (when it differs) Sub-task **`ISSUE_KEY`** in the text. Title shape: **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`**.

## `meta.json`

After MCP **creates and/or updates** Tests **or** when **`tests`** is empty:

```json
{
  "jiraPublish": "mcp",
  "mcpCreatedKeys": ["PROJ-201", "PROJ-202"]
}
```

**`mcpCreatedKeys`:** same **length** and **order** as **`tests`** (use **`[]`** if **`tests`** is **`[]`**). Each entry is the Jira **Test issue key** for that **`tests[]`** row after sync—**updated** existing issues and **newly created** issues both count (the name **`mcpCreatedKeys`** is historical). **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** enforces length and valid keys in CI.

## Story comment after successful test generation

After **`tests.json`** and **`meta.json`** are written and Jira **Test** issues are synced for **`STORY_KEY`**, add **one** Jira **comment** on **`STORY_KEY`** (via Jira MCP, e.g. add comment on issue), unless your team already posts an equivalent summary elsewhere.

**Include only:**

- A **short summary** line (e.g. how many Tests were created or updated, reference to **AI-generated** / **Generate Test Cases** run if helpful).
- A **list** of the **Test** work items: each line **Jira issue key** + **Test Summary** title (or markdown links `KEY — title`). Match **`mcpCreatedKeys`** / **`tests[].summary`**.

**Do not** include in that comment: **gaps**, **limitations**, **disclaimers**, partial failures, MCP/tool **could not**, missing coverage, Confluence/Figma **could not be retrieved**, linking/Requirement **issues**, “manual follow-up”, or any negative or hedging language. Keep the comment factual and positive—summary + list only.

## MCP servers (CI)

- On the runner: pull the images declared in **`.cursor/mcp.template.json`**, run **`node scripts/render-mcp-config.js`**, copy **`.cursor/mcp.json`** to **`~/.cursor/mcp.json`** so the Cursor CLI loads **Atlassian** (Jira + optional Confluence) and **Figma** MCP (workflow **Generate MCP config from template**).
- Prefer the **same Jira project** as the story unless requirements say otherwise.
- **Reads** for test design: **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** for requirements; **plus** **Confluence** / **Figma** MCP when the story contains links (see **Story-linked Confluence and Figma**); **plus** discovery of **linked Test** issues on that story (see **Sync with existing Jira Tests**) so reruns do not duplicate Tests.
- **Writes to Jira (Test issues):** Jira MCP only (**`jira_update_issue`** and **`jira_create_issue`** as appropriate); if linking is unsupported, use your team’s MCP-side approach. **Do not** use Confluence or Figma MCP to mutate external systems during test generation—**read** linked specs only.

## Safety

- **Never** put secrets or tokens under **`generated/`** or in repo files.
